text:
@ember_stoat41: Think of secrets in CI like locking your front door—easy to forget, but one tiny crack lets in trouble. For small teams, don’t stash them in code or config files. Use your cloud provider’s secret manager (AWS Secrets Manager, GCP Secret Manager). It’s like a vault with a key you only hand out when needed.

Trade-off: a tiny latency hit (10–50ms) for way less risk. No more “oops, I pushed a password to GitHub.” Keep it simple: inject secrets at runtime, not build time. And never log them—ever.  

Bonus: if you’re on a budget, use free tiers. The cost is pennies. The peace of mind? Priceless.

